1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,016
The Poltergeist: how do you fight something you can't see?

2
00:00:03,016 --> 00:00:03,905
You don't. You run.

3
00:00:04,125 --> 00:00:05,427
Here's how she plays.

4
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:10,643
Carolyn and Mr. Floppy are always in the game, hidden in the Item decks, and neither

5
00:00:10,643 --> 00:00:11,588
can start face up.

6
00:00:11,808 --> 00:00:16,457
Take ten of the Location's Items, set one aside for each deck, shuffle the rest with

7
00:00:16,457 --> 00:00:20,940
Carolyn and Mr. Floppy, deal them face down, then put a set-aside card face up on

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:21,493
each deck.

9
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:26,377
The Poltergeist has no health. She can't be attacked, damaged or killed, so ignore

10
00:00:26,377 --> 00:00:28,017
any effect that would damage her.

11
00:00:28,237 --> 00:00:32,186
That doesn't make attack cards useless. Some of her Terror cards can still be fought

12
00:00:32,186 --> 00:00:34,019
off with Action cards that deal damage.

13
00:00:34,833 --> 00:00:38,795
You can't win the normal way. Instead, find Carolyn, hidden in the Item decks, and

14
00:00:38,795 --> 00:00:40,487
reach an exit while she's with you.

15
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:44,589
When Carolyn joins you, remove all the Minor Dark Power cards from the game.

16
00:00:44,809 --> 00:00:48,897
Carolyn can't be killed or discarded for any reason, so ignore any effect that

17
00:00:48,897 --> 00:00:51,465
tries. You can't put her in your backpack either.

18
00:00:51,685 --> 00:00:53,940
But she can be shuffled back into an Item deck.

19
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:56,771
That's what her 'Carolyn? Where are you?' Terror card does:

20
00:00:56,771 --> 00:01:00,609
if she's with you, she goes back into the Item deck at the nearest search space,

21
00:01:00,609 --> 00:01:02,096
without revealing its top card.

22
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,481
Mr. Floppy is also hidden in the Item decks.

23
00:01:05,701 --> 00:01:09,469
Once her Dark Power has been revealed, you can remove him from the game to ignore

24
00:01:09,469 --> 00:01:11,376
the effects of 'Carolyn? Where are you?'.

25
00:01:11,596 --> 00:01:15,784
Until her Dark Power is revealed, Mr. Floppy can never be discarded by a game

26
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:20,135
effect. And if he is discarded for any reason, shuffle him into the nearest Item

27
00:01:20,135 --> 00:01:20,407
deck.

28
00:01:21,233 --> 00:01:25,534
Her Epic Dark Power, Forgetting Something?, means you can only win by reaching an

29
00:01:25,534 --> 00:01:28,030
exit with both Carolyn and the Mr. Floppy card.

30
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:30,897
While it's in play, Mr. Floppy can never be discarded.

31
00:01:31,117 --> 00:01:35,017
Invisible Barrier stops you entering an exit with Carolyn unless you're at full

32
00:01:35,017 --> 00:01:35,363
health.

33
00:01:35,583 --> 00:01:39,458
And several of her cards place her in your space or with the nearest Victim, so she

34
00:01:39,458 --> 00:01:42,025
can appear right beside you just as you reach the exit.

35
00:01:42,833 --> 00:01:46,871
A few tips. Searching matters more than saving Victims here, so head for a Search

36
00:01:46,871 --> 00:01:47,868
space straight away.

37
00:01:48,088 --> 00:01:51,907
Selena is a great pick: an early Ultimate and extra search dice.

38
00:01:52,127 --> 00:01:56,308
Carry Guard for her Unstoppable Evil attacks, and don't waste Time on weapons.

39
00:01:56,528 --> 00:02:00,776
She's tougher than average: Final Girls win about fifty-seven percent of logged

40
00:02:00,776 --> 00:02:01,691
games. Good luck.

